# Placement implementation

Typed fields only. `source` is provenance, never a switch.

## Home

- `isHomeSpotlightItem`: dated obligation, this week. Cap `HOME_VISIBLE_MAX` (5).
- Rank with `compareHomeActions` only. Do not put See-all ids first because they were off Home last visit (`rankHomeSpotlightCards`).
- `isAdminActionTitle` (form / RSVP / payment) can be Home. `isEventKitTitle` is packing — not a standalone Home card, even if dated.
- `asHomeNeededNowCards`: this-week event with a Home-due child, or a Home-due parent with packing, is **one Home card**. Kit folds into that checklist. Do not also Radar-group the same cluster.

## Radar

- Holds; upcoming named `occurrence`s (`titleNamesAttendableEvent`, day not past); packing kit under a live parent; far-dated Home overflow (`selectRadarWatch`). Generic meetings stay Schedule-only.
- An **occurrence** / dated **context_only** keeps its work nested even when there is only one child (same shape as Schedule). Kit under a form still needs 2+ lines to collapse.
- Packing under a **hold** does not get its own card — the hold is enough.
- List-bound if `collection_id`, `kind=list_item`, or the parent has a collection.
- Never bare Card/Present/Gift, never children of a closed or missing parent.

## Lists

`organizeStandaloneItems`: undated chat/manual → General to do or Shopping. Named `occurrence` / dated `context_only` stay off lists. Never a custom list from child count.

## Tests

Stable Home vs See all; this-week gala is one Home card with form + kit; helmet hold without buy-child; list-bound todos off Radar. Do not delete those assertions.
